A||||7||Fiero_24||Low oil pressure.||||5||
Z||000000||Fiero_24||12-23-2001||11:26 PM||||I just drove my Fiero with the new performance rebuild for the first time.  at a stop or at idle after the car warms up I have little oil pressure.  It goes so low to the point that the oil pressure light flickers on and off.  I have the high flow oil pump in there.<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/driverside41.jpg"> <BR>  <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fiero_24" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/fiero_24</A> <BR>1987 GT||||reg||5
Z||000001||lowfierogt||12-23-2001||11:55 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Fiero_24:<BR><B>I just drove my Fiero with the new performance rebuild for the first time.  at a stop or at idle after the car warms up I have little oil pressure.  It goes so low to the point that the oil pressure light flickers on and off.  I have the high flow oil pump in there.<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>My 86 GT has the same problem.  I was thinking the car was idling to low.   im going to turn the idle up on TB.<P><P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://lowfierogt.no-ip.com/lowfierogtsig.gif">          <BR>http://lowfierogt.no-ip.com<BR>84 SE<BR>85 GT <BR>2 X 86 1/2 GT<BR>87 coupe V6 300k miles<BR>87 coupe 4 auto, 68k M<BR>88 Formula 5 speed T-Top||||reg||1
Z||000002||FieroMontreal||12-24-2001||12:11 AM||||I have the same problem.. I think.. My car has 128000 KM ... not to bad.. I added a lot of new stuff.. When the car is in Motion or when its cold on idle it will have good/high oil pressure... when its hot and I'm stoped at a light the pressure will drop and my light will come on.. I dunno what to do!! My engine seems to be running great.. argh.. helpppp!! lol<P>------------------<BR> -Alex <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sigfieromontrealholidays.gif"> <BR>1986 Fiero GT, STOCK Wingless, <BR>President of FieroMontreal... <A HREF="http://www.fieromontreal.com" TARGET=_blank>www.fieromontreal.com</A> <BR>and Regional Director of CFOG-I for Eastern Canada.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Fiero_24||12-24-2001||09:01 AM||||I hate these darn Fiero Gremlins.  My car is going to the mechanic for new roller rockers.  I am going to have him take a look at the oil pressure problem.  ||||reg||8
Z||000004||Dslice||12-24-2001||01:55 PM||||This happens to me once and a while too. I usually check the oil and add a little. You could try using a heavier weight oil or it may just be a bad oil pressure sending unit. I replaced one of those once also. Then again it may just be an evil spirt. It scares the crap out of me cause if I do have low oil pressure, yikes! There must be a way to test the pressure with some pressure testing to tool.<P>------------------<BR>Rick<P>86GT<BR>84COUP<BR>http://home.mn.rr.com/gmfierogt||||reg||1
Z||000005||lawrence||12-24-2001||02:22 PM||||Put 20W50 in there and your pressure will go up quite a bit.  I've always used 20W50 in my cars.  I'm not sure that it's any better, but I definitely FEEL better.<P>Good luck,<P>-L<BR> <A HREF="http://members.nccw.net/webe/products" TARGET=_blank>http://members.nccw.net/webe/products</A>  - Sequential Turn Signals||||reg||1
Z||000006||Fiero_24||12-24-2001||02:45 PM||||20-50 in a brand new motor?  That seems a little odd for a new motor.  I have changed the oil pressure sending unit.<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/driverside41.jpg"> <BR>  <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fiero_24" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/fiero_24</A> <BR>1987 GT||||reg||1
Z||000007||CanadianGT||12-24-2001||03:46 PM||||It may be a faulty oil pressure sending unit, and I am not sure if fieros have these, but it could also be that your oil pressure relief valve is stuck wide open, or partly open, thus draining your oil at idle back to the sump...In adition, it could also be that after your oil heats up, it thins out which is natural for a drop in pressure.  But that is not usual on a car with a fresh rebuild.  I would suggest doing a maunual oil pressure test just to make sure the guage is telling you the proper info.<BR>Just a thought.<BR>PeAcE<BR>Kyle<p>[This message has been edited by CanadianGT (edited 12-24-2001).]||||reg||1
